  "rationale": "first-request: complete-request wall 377.028205 to 377.891453 seconds; allocated bytes 2494289512 to 2494199808; process peak 10229989376 to 9098006528; denoiser HtoD 3207992256 to 2786513856 bytes and 402 to 252 calls. repeat-request: complete-request wall 379.221847 to 379.700269 seconds; allocated bytes 2467028048 to 2466955560; process peak 10229989376 to 9098006528; denoiser HtoD 3201700800 to 2780222400 bytes and 400 to 250 calls. first-request wall_ns increased from 377028205000 to 377891452900 repeat-request wall_ns increased from 379221846500 to 379700269500 The frozen decision uses both full-request lifetime states; the small G4 case and its second-upload ablation verify output and causal transfer counts. Host copy API time includes validation/blocking, not isolated GPU-active DMA. Separate driver peaks are not a combined device peak. Host process peaks include the earlier G4 check. Ordinary host applications and file cache remain uncontrolled; this comparison does not establish a population speedup. The independently verified conditioning-pair ownership repair remains in either decision. After rejecting the transfer candidate, a regression also confirmed that the original single-branch method accepted released conditioning. The retained implementation adds session ownership, retained-handle and closed-session checks while restoring the original step uploads; its numerical and lifecycle references pass separately. Full-request timings belong to the recorded baseline and candidate snapshots and were not reacquired after those handle checks. No pinned-memory allocator, asynchronous scheduler or geometry-specific threshold was added.",
